#macro ChoiceStatCheck(statName, statValue) \
    $data   CheckStat = "$statName" \
    $data   CheckStatValue = $statValue
#macro ChoiceTime(time) \
    $data   TIme = $time

#basePath TestChapter

:: Preload
@function    ChapterPreload

$call SetBackground("bg/Nightmare.png")

// #region Opening

:: Start
@trigger    ChapterStart
@cutscene

{@}     They're late.
        Those two asked you to meet and they're <i>late</i>.
        At least, you think they're late.
$choice .Start.Late.A; Who?
$choice .Start.Late.B; I think?
$choose branch
{@}     Might as well pass the time until they arrive.

$choice .Start.Bench; Sit on the bench.
$choice .Start.Railing; Lean over the railing.
$choose branch

{@}     ...
        Why did you come to this town?
$choice .Start.Arrival.A; To investigate
$choice .Start.Arrival.B; To escape
$choice .Start.Arrival.C; I don't remember.
$choose branch

{@}     ...
        Okay, they're officially too late.
        The anglers might have just... forgotten about you.
        That's fine. You can still enjoy the sights.
$choice .Start.EndOfDock; Walk to the end of the dock.
$choose branch

$goto .WakeUp

:: Start.Late.A
{@}     The anglers.
        They said they had "something important to show you."
        And it had to be in person, for whatever reason.

:: Start.Late.B
{@}     You could be wrong.
        You've been known to forget things from time to time.
        But you're pretty sure the anglers were supposed to be here by now.

:: Start.Bench
{@}     You park yourself on a nearby bench.
        The boards creak softly in response.

:: Start.Railing
{@}     You lean your weight on the railing.
        Some rust flakes off on your skin.
        
:: Start.Arrival.A
$set local:dream.arrival.reason = "investigate"
{@}     That's right.
        You were sent to look into...
$choice .Start.Arrival.A.Fish; Fish populations
$choice .Start.Arrival.A.Food; Local restaurants
$choice .Start.Arrival.A.Joke; A murder! Ooh spooky

:: Start.Arrival.A.Fish
$set local:dream.fish = true
{@}     Fish populations.
        They were trending downward, if I recall.
        You are an... ecologist.
$call AdjustStat(Research, 1)

:: Start.Arrival.A.Food
$set local:dream.restaurant = true
{@}     Local restaurants.
        There's an up-and-coming poutine place downtown.
        You are a... famous food critic. Sure.
$call AdjustStat(Innovate, 1)

:: Start.Arrival.A.Joke
$set local:dream.crows = true
{@}     A... murder.
        Not sure what crows have to do with this, but okay.
        You are an... ornithologist. Fine.
$call AdjustStat(Communicate, 1)

:: Start.Arrival.B
$set local:dream.arrival.reason = "escape"
{@}     That's right.
        You wanted to escape from...
$choice .Start.Arrival.B.Job; A dead-end job
$choice .Start.Arrival.B.Brooding; Myself (oh so brooding)
$choice .Start.Arrival.B.Joke; ...A giant trout?

:: Start.Arrival.B.Job
$set local:dream.broke = true
{@}     A dead-end job.
        A living wage was out-of-reach there, and rent just kept climbing.
        You hope... to make rent out here.
$call AdjustStat(Ranger, 1)

:: Start.Arrival.B.Brooding
$set local:dream.brooding = true
{@}     ...Yourself.
        A little on-the-nose I think.
        But sure I can roll with that.
$call AdjustStat(Communicate, 1)

:: Start.Arrival.B.Joke
$set local:dream.trout = true
{@}     A... giant trout?
        ...What?
        Okay fine a giant trout was chasing you and you fled heroically.
$call AdjustStat(Tech, 1)

:: Start.Arrival.C
$set level:dream.arrival.reason = "unknown"
{@}     You don't remember.
        How curious.

:: Start.EndOfDock
{@}     You see yourself in the murky water.

$choice .Start.EndOfDock.A; She stares back.
$choice .Start.EndOfDock.B; They stare back.
$choice .Start.EndOfDock.C; He stares back.
$choose branch

{@}     {pg His|Her|Their} face suddenly sinks beneath the waves.
        Your heart follows suit and crashes to your stomach.
        The stench of rotting fish wafts up. You suppress the urge to gag.
        The surface of the water begins to writhe and contort.

:: Start.EndOfDock.A
$set global:gender="f"

:: Start.EndOfDock.B
$set global:gender="x"

:: Start.EndOfDock.C
$set global:gender="m"

// #endregion

// #region Bedroom

:: WakeUp
@cutscene

$call ClearVisibleLines()
$call SetBackground("bg/Room.png")
{@}     Reality arrives swiftly and disorientingly.
{@Player}   Ugh, haven't had one of those in ages.{auto}
$if local:dream.restaurant
            I could really go for some fries right now...
$elseif local:dream.crows
            And what was that about birds...
$elseif local:dream.fish
            Upcoming job's really got me stressed out...
$elseif local:dream.broke
            Finances haven't been that tight, right?
$elseif local:dream.brooding
            Thought I was over that by now...
$elseif local:dream.trout
            Utter nonsense...
$else
            So strange...
$endif
{@Player}   Welp, another one for my therapist.

{@}     On your desk, you spot several notes you've taken.

$call GiveEvidenceCard("Evidence-Lamprey-Discovered")

// #endregion 

// #region Docks
 
$goto .TravelDocks

:: TravelDocks

{@}     Your remember hearing about Sea Lampreys. 
        The Anglers by the docks were making whispers of them. 
        
$choice .Docks.A; Guess I should go ask those anglers. 

:: .Docks.A

{@} 
        You make your way to the docks.

$goto .AnglersDocks

:: AnglersDocks

{@}     As you approach the docks, you see two Anglers. 

{@Angler1}      
        Never thought we'd see the day. 
{@Angler2}      
        I've been tellin' ya, they gettin' bolder. 

{@}     
        You decide to say hello. 
{@Player}   
        Hi there! 

{@}    
        They don't seem to notice you. 

$choice .Docks.Attention.A; <i>say nothing and slowly approach<i>
$choice .Docks.Attention.B; Uhm... hi? Is everything alright? 
$choice .Docks.Attention.C; Is this how Anglers typically greet people?
$choose branch

{@Angler1}     
        Take a closer look. 

{@}     He holds the fish up to you. 
        You notice that the bite marks are nothing familiar to the region.
        Infact, they're uniquely circular.  

{@Angler2} 
        They have been on many of the fish we catch. Whitefish and Walleye. 

{@Angler1} 
        And Lamprey feed on them. 
        
$call GiveEvidenceCard("Evidence-Lake-Whitefish")

$call GiveEvidenceCard("Evidence-Lake-Trout")

{@Angler1} 
        A good chunk of those fish wind up dead. 

{@Angler2}
        Dead fish means rotten fish. 

{@Angler1} 
        Rotten fish means you can't sell the fish. 

{@Player} 
        Not only are you guys out of your jobs, but the entire town's economy is at threat.

{@}     The anglers nod their heads in unison. 
        You think for a moment, understanding the gravity of the situation.

{@Player} 
        What can I do to help? 

{@Angler1}   
        Talking to someone who knows more about Sea Lamprey's may be a good idea. 
        Maybe going to the <i>DNR Office<i> or even the <i>University Researh Lab<i>. 

{@Angler2} 
        Going to the <i>Town Hall<i> may be a good idea as well. 

{@} 
        You think to yourself, where would be the best next place to go. 

$choice .DNR.Office; DNR Office
$choice .University.Research.Lab; The Research Lab
$choice .Town.Hall; Town Hall
$choose branch

:: Docks.Attention.A
{@}     As you approach, you notice the Anglers staring at a whitefish.
        On the whitefish is a bite mark. 
        Before you could study it further, Angler 1 and Angler 2 turn towards you startled. 

{@Angler1}      Holy worms kid! Can't sneak on an old soul like that! 
{@Angler2}      Ye' tryin' to kill us? 

{@Player}       No! Sorry, I... just... what's with the fish? 
 
:: Docks.Attention.B

{@Angler1}      Huh? Oh kid! Nice to see ya! To answer your question...
{@Angler2}      Nay, things be not well... 

{@Player}       How come? 

:: Docks.Attention.C

{@} Both the Anglers turn your way. 

{@Angler2} Aye. When the lady of the lake be singing her solemn song. 
{@Angler1} ...Pardon him. But he's right, it's a solemn day indeed. 

{@Player} What's wrong?

:: DNR.Office

{@Player} The DNR Office seems the best place to go. 

{@Angler1} Good choice, they may provide more info on what's going on. 

:: University.Research.Lab

{@Player} The University Research Lab. I remember hearing they were studying lampreys. 

{@Angler2} Aye, they might put a stop to this. 

:: Town.Hall

{@Player} I can always bring it to Town Hall. 

{@Angler1} Ah. Politics. Have fun convincing them to do anything. 

:: Town.Hall.Location 


:: University.Research.Lab.Location


:: DNR.LocationS


